<h1>Automatic Tray Loading &amp; Unloading Systems</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">An automatic tray loader places product into trays without hand-packing, and an automatic tray unloader does the reverse: it removes product from trays or separates stacked trays for reuse. A loading cell combines a tray denester, product infeed conveyor, placement mechanism (cam-driven pick-and-place, servo gantry, or delta robot), and outfeed conveyor. Placement method is set by throughput, SKU count, and product fragility, all compared below.</p>
<h2 id="automatic-tray-loaders">What Is an Automatic Tray Loader?</h2>
<p>An automatic tray loader is a machine that loads trays automatically: it takes product from an infeed conveyor and places it into tray cavities in a set pattern, with no hand-packing. Every automatic tray loader has the same four parts: a tray denester or destacker that feeds empty trays, a product infeed that presents product to the pick zone, a placement mechanism (cam-driven pick-and-place, servo gantry, or delta robot), and an outfeed that carries filled trays to a sealer, lidder, wrapper, or case packer. The placement mechanism is the main choice and is compared below.</p>
